[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to file upload handling, specifically an Unrestricted File Upload vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when the application allows users to upload files without adequately validating the file type or content. In this case, the API is designed to accept zip files, but if the implementation does not enforce strict checks on the uploaded file's format or contents, it could lead to the execution of malicious files or scripts contained within the zip archive. This lack of validation can expose the server to various attacks, including remote code execution or denial of service, as attackers may exploit the file upload feature to upload harmful files disguised as legitimate zip files.

